Subject: A compare-and-branch on a frame local polls at its real target

What this does
  regvm_t_branch_cmp_loc_reg no longer calls REGVM_DRC_BACKEDGE itself before T_NEXT: T_NEXT already runs the back-edge poll, on the full offset (the instruction's size plus the branch offset).

Why we need it
  The extra call used the bare branch offset, which this instruction counts from its end, so when the poll fired (the interrupt countdown reaching zero, or the deferred-count safepoint) the loop resumed ten bytes before its target, in the middle of an earlier instruction, and the dispatch loop met a 0 byte: "InternalError: register VM: unimplemented opcode 0" on JetStream 3 typescript-lib (forEachChildRecursively: `for (let t = e.length - 1; t >= 0; --t)`). It also counted the interrupt down twice per taken back edge. Repro: tests/differential/corpus/backedge-poll-local-compare.js.

Soundness
  Every other threaded branch polls only through T_NEXT/T_BR_NEXT, with the offset they continue at; this handler now does the same, so the poll and the continuation agree on the target.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index a012267..b0bb73c 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -34597,4 +34597,2 @@ static uint8_t *REGVM_CC regvm_t_branch_cmp_loc_reg(REGVM_ARGS)
-        if (unlikely(r ^ ((sub & REG_CMP_INVERT) != 0))) {
-            REGVM_DRC_BACKEDGE(ctx, off);
-            T_NEXT(T_SZ_BURT + off);
-        }
+        if (unlikely(r ^ ((sub & REG_CMP_INVERT) != 0)))
+            T_NEXT(T_SZ_BURT + off); /* T_NEXT runs the back-edge poll on the target it continues at */
